   This posting is NOT pro or con the proposal and
   NOT A CHANGE PROPOSAL, just a technical feasibility study.

   If we overload NOI and make the following changes to the YACC grammar,
   we can express both an origin and an offset:

C time_1030               :  time_distance_1036
C                         |  time_distance_1036  time_A_1031
                          |  time_A_1031
                          ;

  time_offset_1033        :  time_direction_1035
C                         |  time_direction_1035 time_distance_1036
                          ;

+ time_distance_1036      :  ZI_624
+                         |  ZI_624 NOI_585 sentence_40 BO_508


C space_A_1042          :  space_distance_1049
C                       |  space_distance_1049  space_B_1043
                        |  space_B_1043
                        ;

  space_offset_1045       :  space_direction_1048
C                         |  space_direction_1048  space_distance_1049

+ space_distance_1049   :  VA_613
+                       |  VA_613 NOI_585 sentence_40 BO_508


   A more general form would replace 'NOI_585 sentence_40' with
   'relative_clauses_121'.

   Corresponding changes could be made to the grammar of VEhA/ZEhA.

   All these modifications pass YACC without conflicts.

   VA/ZI+NOI is more verbose than xe'i but also more expressive as it
   combines subjective and objective distances.

   Examples:

     *   mi pu zanoi nanca lipimu bo klama la glazgov.
     *   mi zano'u pimu loi mi gu'arna'a bo vi gunka
     *   mi xabju vanoi mitre lipaxaki'o bo la'o sy Helsinki sy

